# DigiSwasthya Product Definition Document (PDD)

# Part 2 — User Roles & Responsibilities

---

# Purpose

This section defines every user role within DigiSwasthya.

It explains:

- Who the user is.
- Why they use the platform.
- What business problems they solve.
- What responsibilities they have.
- What information belongs to them.
- What they are allowed to do.
- What they are not allowed to do.

This section defines responsibilities only.

It does **not** define features or screens.

Those are defined in later sections.

---

# User Roles

The platform currently supports three primary user roles.

1. Pharmacy
2. Stockist
3. Platform Administrator

No other roles currently exist within the product.

Doctors, patients, medical representatives, manufacturers, transporters, and consumers are outside the current product scope.

---

# Role 1 — Pharmacy

## Overview

A Pharmacy is a licensed business that purchases pharmaceutical products from one or more stockists for resale or dispensing.

The pharmacy is the buyer within the B2B relationship.

The pharmacy uses DigiSwasthya to digitally manage purchasing, inventory, payments, supplier relationships, and retail operations.

---

## Primary Goals

A pharmacy wants to:

- Find reliable stockists.
- Purchase medicines.
- Receive products.
- Maintain inventory.
- Track outstanding orders.
- Pay suppliers.
- Return damaged or expired goods.
- Monitor business performance.
- Reduce manual work.

---

## Responsibilities

A pharmacy is responsible for:

- Maintaining accurate business information.
- Maintaining valid licenses.
- Ordering products responsibly.
- Receiving deliveries correctly.
- Reporting shortages or damaged products.
- Making payments.
- Managing inventory.
- Managing pharmacy staff.
- Following pharmaceutical regulations.

---

## Business Ownership

A pharmacy owns and manages:

- Business profile.
- Business documents.
- Staff.
- Delivery addresses.
- Internal inventory.
- Customer sales.
- Purchase history.
- Payment history.
- Return requests.
- Wishlist.
- Business settings.

---

## Relationships

A pharmacy can establish business relationships with multiple stockists.

A pharmacy cannot purchase products from a stockist unless a valid business relationship exists.

---

## Permissions

A pharmacy should be able to:

- Register.
- Complete verification.
- Manage its profile.
- Manage staff.
- Search for stockists.
- Request connections.
- View connected stockists.
- Browse catalogues.
- Place orders.
- Track orders.
- Receive deliveries.
- Record received quantities.
- Make payments.
- Submit payment proof.
- Raise return requests.
- Receive credit notes.
- View notifications.
- Communicate with stockists.
- View analytics.
- Manage settings.

---

## Restrictions

A pharmacy should not be able to:

- Approve its own verification.
- Approve payments.
- Modify invoices issued by stockists.
- Edit completed deliveries.
- Delete financial records.
- Access another pharmacy's data.
- View private stockist information.
- Purchase products without verification.
- Purchase products from disconnected stockists.

---

## Success

A pharmacy successfully completes its business cycle when it can:

Connect

↓

Order

↓

Receive

↓

Pay

↓

Return (if required)

↓

Continue purchasing

without requiring external communication channels.

